  "declared_proposition": "For a finite deficit sequence d and anchors partitioning the index interval, every point is at most the maximum anchor value plus the largest accumulated absolute first difference between neighboring anchors. Therefore anchor_max+variation_radius<1 is a rigorous pointwise Goldbach certificate. No normalized Lp moment with fixed finite p can replace local control: one unit spike in a block of length L has normalized Lp norm L^(-1/p) tending to zero while retaining one exact exception.",
